what The four rune bindings all derive their head roster from glow/tokens.rye match_rune2's pairs table, and the lexer recognizes two rune-shaped two-byte heads ABOVE that branch -- == (double_equals, the tall-form terminator, consumed by rune_shape.rye at two sites and standing in 105 tracked .glow sources) and :: (the comment head). == is named in none of the three documents the guard binds while its partner -- is named in all three. Derive the outside heads from the lexer too and publish them as their own reading.
claim bakery-rishi-make-pen
seat bakery
stamp 20260915.233209
epoch 1789529529
paths rishi/src/main.rye tools/r/rishi_make_pen_witness.rish tools/fixtures/r/rishi_make_pen_control.sh
what Rishi already owns a CleanupRegistry that releases on normal return, refusal, exit, HUP, INT and TERM -- the card's standing claim that Rishi has no trap at all is false, and the registry's one kind is empty_dir registered only by acquire-lock. Add a make-pen expression builtin: the runtime creates the directory itself under TMPDIR and registers it for bounded recursive release, so it can only ever remove a directory it made in this process and never a caller-supplied path. Turns the 336 unreleased_on_refusal and the 16 never_removed Rishi pens from a language gap into a one-line cure.
