claim bakery-ryekey-toolchain-spelling
seat bakery
stamp 20260916.023136
epoch 1789540296
paths rye/src/main.rye tools/fixtures/r/ryekey_control.sh
what The build receipt keys on the toolchain PATH STRING beside its content, so one pinned compiler wears four live spellings and four different keys -- measured on this tree: RYE_ZIG absolute gives bdd5d31e, the compiler's own default resolution gives c626631a, same 172MB binary, same sources, same flags. The tree spells the pin 980 times relative, 34 absolute, 13 through a root variable, and leaves it unset everywhere rye_build.sh runs. Drop the path and the library path from the key, keep both content hashes, bump the marker to v6, and turn control leg 8 around with its reason written.
claim nobody here has proposed. Build a scan that reads the tree's own tracked files under two keys -- SHA3-512 (the tree's own digest, avalanching) and a locality key derived from path structure -- and measures the SAME two properties against each: adjacency (do same-room pairs land near?) and evenness (chi-squared over the fold). The trade is the finding: avalanche buys evenness and destroys adjacency. Whether a locality key can buy adjacency without losing evenness is the falsifier, and it is answerable on this pier today with no board and no new hardware.
